In short: food and beverage businesses with annual revenue of up to S$10,000,000 may use the software for
their own outlets free of charge; system vendors, resellers and hosting providers may not commercialise it
without a separate commercial license. The full terms below are what apply.

1. Definitions

"Licensor" means Leonard Chow Yi Ding.

"Software" means the Hawkerline source code, documentation and other files distributed with this license,
and any modified version of them.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license. "Your Affiliates" means any
entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with You, where "control" means owning
more than 50% of the voting interests or having the power to direct management.

"Annual Revenue" means the total gross revenue of You and Your Affiliates combined, from all sources, for the
most recently completed financial year, converted into Singapore dollars at a reasonable prevailing rate.
If You have not yet completed a financial year, Annual Revenue means Your reasonably projected gross revenue
for Your first financial year.

"Eligible Merchant" means a business that operates restaurants, cafés, food stalls, kiosks, bakeries,
take-away or delivery kitchens or other food and beverage outlets, and whose Annual Revenue is not more than
S$10,000,000 (ten million Singapore dollars).

"Own Use" means using the Software to run the Eligible Merchant's own outlets and brands, including taking
orders and payments from that merchant's own customers, running its kitchen, point of sale, menu and staff
functions, and connecting the merchant's own AI agents and tools to it.

"Commercial Provider" means anyone who offers software, systems or services to other businesses, including
POS, ordering or restaurant-software vendors, SaaS and hosting providers, resellers, distributors, agencies,
system integrators and franchisors acting for their franchisees.

2. Free use by Eligible Merchants

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants an Eligible Merchant a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free,
non-transferable license to use, copy, modify, install, deploy and self-host the Software for its Own Use,
on infrastructure it controls or that is provided to it in its own name.

3. Contractors working for an Eligible Merchant

An Eligible Merchant may engage employees, freelancers or contractors to install, configure, modify, operate
and maintain the Software for that merchant's Own Use. Such persons may charge the merchant for their time
and work. They may not, under this license, sell, license, rent or otherwise charge for the Software itself,
or run one deployment of the Software for more than one unrelated business. Operating one Eligible
Merchant's own deployment in this way is not a hosted or managed service under section 5(b); offering such
work as a standard product or package to many businesses is.

4. Non-commercial use

Anyone may use, copy and modify the Software for personal use, evaluation, testing, research, teaching and
learning, and for use by non-profit organisations, as long as that use is not for the commercial advantage
of a Commercial Provider.

5. What requires a separate commercial license

The following are not permitted under this license and require a written commercial license from the
Licensor:

  (a) selling, reselling, licensing, sublicensing, renting, leasing or otherwise charging for the Software or
      any modified version of it;
  (b) offering the Software, or functionality substantially derived from it, to third parties as a hosted,
      managed, multi-tenant, white-label or software-as-a-service product;
  (c) bundling, embedding or pre-installing the Software in a product, device or service that is sold or
      provided by a Commercial Provider to other businesses;
  (d) use of the Software by or for a business whose Annual Revenue is more than S$10,000,000, other than
      the non-commercial uses in section 4 and the transition period in section 6.

6. Growing above the threshold

If You were an Eligible Merchant and Your Annual Revenue later exceeds S$10,000,000, You may continue to use
the Software under this license for 90 days after the end of the financial year in which the threshold was
exceeded. To continue after that period You need a commercial license.

